  "predeclared_hypothesis": "Group the five visible faces by genuine orientation, prompting one opposite-face complement7 per displayed face. False exhaustiveness gives5*7-(1+2+4+6+2)=20; the missing left side-pair contributes7.",
  "material_difference_from_old": "Old Solid192 was screened with no saved candidate or calls. It rejected changing pips or highlighting only the shared seam. This new design never marks a pip: it assigns two open existing boundary edges to EACH of five visible faces, matching top-to-top and front-to-front across the dice. It targets the precise mistake that the five opposite faces exhaust the unseen faces, omitting the remaining unseen opposite pair of the left die. Thus35-15=20 rather than42-15=27.",
  "primary_unique_math_proof": "Each ordinary die has total1+2+3+4+5+6=21 spots. Actual source/formal show left top1 and front2, and right top4,front6,side2; visible total15. Both dice total42, so all unseen spots total27. Opposite lookup alone accounts for left bottom6+rear5=11 and right bottom3+rear1+left5=9, total20. The left die also has two unseen opposite side faces summing7; including them gives27. This uses only ordinary dice and actual visible faces, without assuming hidden contact values individually.",
